CSS vs Ncurses terminology

@table @code
@item A_NORMAL
font-weight-normal
visibility-visible
text-decoration-none

@item A_STANDOUT
font-weight-bold
 
@item A_UNDERLINE
text-decoration-underline

@item A_REVERSE
no real analog
color-reverse?

@item A_BLINK
text-decoration-blink

@item A_DIM
font-weight-lighter

@item A_BOLD
font-weight-bold

@item A_PROTECT

@item A_INVIS
visibility-invisible

@item A_ALTCHARSET

@item COLOR_PAIR
background-color
color
border-color
border-{top, right, bottom, left}-color
@end table

There ought to be a function to tell you what STANDOUT does by trying
to compareits terminfo database (capname smso, TCapCode so) with the
others: underline (smul / us), blink (blink / mb), dim (dim / mh),
bold (bold / md). 


infocmp is the program to make terminfo legible

For xterm, A_STANDOUT is A_REVERSE.

For curses, there are two ways to give colors.  @code{color: red} and
@code{color: rgb(255, 0, 0)}

